# Example ReRDMFT input file: carbon monoxide (R = 1.128 Angstrom), cc-pVDZ basis (co-cc-pvdz.gbs, from
# https://www.basissetexchange.org/, includes D shells), GNOF with 3 coupling subspaces of 2 orbitals each,
# FULL_OPTIMIZATION with the second-order NEO orbital optimizer and CHOLESKY TRUE: the AO integrals are decomposed
# once into Cholesky vectors and nothing of size n^4 is ever stored (see README.md, CHOLESKY).
# X2C path (complex spinors, Kramers-restricted rotations). Measured: ~2.3 min, ~140 MB peak, converges in 7
# macro-iterations to -113.0844731 Ha (a genuine minimum). Follow the run with `tail -f
# co_ccpvdz_x2c_gnof_neo_cholesky.live`.
NELEC 14
BASIS co-cc-pvdz.gbs
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 3
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO
CHOLESKY TRUE

GEOMETRY
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.128000
END
